    <item>
      <title>Daily Podcast 2026-10-15</title>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://github.com/vllorens/microbiome_digest/releases/download/episode-2026-10-15/podcast_2026-10-15.mp3</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 08:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
      <enclosure url="https://github.com/vllorens/microbiome_digest/releases/download/episode-2026-10-15/podcast_2026-10-15.mp3" length="17839988" type="audio/mpeg" />
      <description>Researchers reviewing the brain‑gut‑microbiome axis report that disrupted bidirectional signaling among the central nervous system, enteric nervous system, immune pathways, and intestinal microbiota underlies both irritable bowel syndrome and depression. | Beta‑hydroxybutyrate (BHB) markedly eases intestinal acute graft‑versus‑host disease by remodeling the gut microbiota‑bile acid axis and blocking the TLR4‑NF‑κB pathway that drives pathogenic Th1 and Th17 T‑cell responses. | Fermenting Sargassum soluble dietary fiber with Bifidobacterium longum boosts its ability to curb oxidative stress and rebalance gut microbes, protecting mice from inflammatory bowel disease.</description>
      <itunes:author>Veronica Llorens</itunes:author>
      <itunes:summary>Researchers reviewing the brain‑gut‑microbiome axis report that disrupted bidirectional signaling among the central nervous system, enteric nervous system, immune pathways, and intestinal microbiota underlies both irritable bowel syndrome and depression. | Beta‑hydroxybutyrate (BHB) markedly eases intestinal acute graft‑versus‑host disease by remodeling the gut microbiota‑bile acid axis and blocking the TLR4‑NF‑κB pathway that drives pathogenic Th1 and Th17 T‑cell responses. | Fermenting Sargassum soluble dietary fiber with Bifidobacterium longum boosts its ability to curb oxidative stress and rebalance gut microbes, protecting mice from inflammatory bowel disease.</itunes:summary>
      <itunes:explicit>false</itunes:explicit>
      <itunes:image href="https://vllorens.github.io/microbiome_digest/cover.png" />
    </item>
